    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "everyone i know expects the 'mask' version of me. if i were real with them, it would just break everything. they'd look at me with pity or fear, and honestly, that sounds more exhausting than just staying quiet. it's like, if the only way to be myself is to be an outcast or a burden, maybe there's just no good way for me to exist in this world. it feels like the struggle is just... inevitable. like it's just my destiny to be miserable or gone.",
